<<.from-version "5.5.0">> The <<.def make-live-reorder-backstop>> [[procedure|Procedures]] renders a drop target covering the whole of a list that is being reordered by dragging, for as long as one of its items is being dragged.

It answers only where the items themselves do not, catching what falls between them: the padding around the list and the ground beyond its ends. As well as letting a drop there land rather than be refused, this is what marks out where the list is, so that a drag crossing such ground is not taken for a drag that has left the list altogether.

<<.tip """This is used internally by the <<.dlink make-live-reorderable-list "make-live-reorderable-list Procedure">> procedure, which renders a whole list and is what you would normally use. Use this one only to build something that procedure cannot.""">>

It takes <<.param list>>, <<.param enable>>, <<.param dragState>>, <<.param dropActions>> and <<.param commit>>, which mean the same as they do for <<.dlink make-live-reorderable-list "make-live-reorderable-list Procedure">>.

It must be rendered inside the element the list is laid out in, which must be positioned, and before the items so that they are drawn on top of it. See DragAndDropMechanism for an overview.
